title: 'pallet-revive: test that operations read and write what they declare'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Adds tests that compare the entries each operation declares with the keys it reads and
      writes. On both the EVM and PolkaVM backends, they cover successful calls (plain, delegate,
      static and with value), a call to an account delegated with EIP-7702, and a contract created
      by another contract. They also cover calls to an account without code, with and without
      value, and value transfers to a contract.

      Also adds checks that a transfer with dust is charged more than one without, and that the
      first frame warms the sender's account info as a write only when the value has dust.

      No runtime behaviour changes, so nothing needs to be migrated.

crates:
  - name: pallet-revive
    bump: none
